WEBVTT

01:13.000 --> 01:16.370
The time is now midnight.

01:16.370 --> 01:20.100
A permit is required to remain outdoors.

01:20.480 --> 01:24.480
Persons without a permit are advised
to return home immediately.

01:24.480 --> 01:26.450
You poor thing...

01:27.320 --> 01:30.940
But your suffering will soon be ended

01:31.390 --> 01:34.820
by the death that awaits you tonight!

01:47.400 --> 01:48.800
Stop!

01:48.800 --> 01:51.000
Hey! What are you doing there?

01:54.340 --> 01:56.140
Are you all right?!

02:00.250 --> 02:04.250
Ninth Night
Blessed are the Impure

02:04.250 --> 02:04.520
Boy, I wish you could have seen me
swooping in and rescuing Nami!

02:04.520 --> 02:07.420
Minakami
Restaurant

02:04.520 --> 02:07.420

Boy, I wish you could have seen me
swooping in and rescuing Nami!

02:07.420 --> 02:10.760
Boy, I wish you could have seen me
swooping in and rescuing Nami!

02:10.760 --> 02:14.250
Fate must have brought us together!

02:16.030 --> 02:17.900
Hey, are you listening?!

02:18.970 --> 02:20.340
We're listening, we're listening.

02:20.340 --> 02:24.340
Thanks so much for sharing, but you know...

02:24.340 --> 02:28.970
It seems just a little too convenient that you
just happened to be passing by!

02:29.840 --> 02:31.850
That's the problem with you amateurs!

02:31.850 --> 02:38.220
We're conducting special patrols in order
to avoid any further mystery killings.

02:38.220 --> 02:41.760
A crime prevention tactic,
resulting in Nami's glorious rescue!

02:41.760 --> 02:45.390
In that case, why isn't there
any news of the incident?

02:45.630 --> 02:47.130
Well, see...

02:47.130 --> 02:49.730
Now, don't give Mr. Shinjo such a hard time.

02:49.730 --> 02:52.600
What? You're taking his side, Nami?

02:52.600 --> 02:55.540
Well, he did save my life!

02:55.540 --> 02:57.300
Of course she is!

02:57.710 --> 03:03.300
I'm Nami's knight in shining armor!
So, about that date you promised me...

03:04.310 --> 03:06.110
All in good time.

03:08.920 --> 03:12.390
Well, well! You still haven't had that date?

03:12.390 --> 03:14.590
Shut up! It's none of your business!

03:14.590 --> 03:17.260
Ha! I see you're all bark and no bite!

03:17.260 --> 03:18.260
What?!

03:18.260 --> 03:21.130
Prove me wrong then,
and bring in the Skull Man!

03:21.130 --> 03:22.430
What do you know, you worthless hack!

03:22.430 --> 03:23.900
Idiots...
What do you know, you worthless hack!

03:25.070 --> 03:26.430
Sheesh...

03:26.430 --> 03:30.730
The press was all over this stuff before,
and now they won't touch it. It's fishy, all right.

03:31.110 --> 03:34.040
Why didn't you ask Miss Nami
about the other day?

03:34.980 --> 03:39.240
She was at the White Bell shrine!
That could be a clue!

03:41.680 --> 03:43.180
Never mind.

03:43.180 --> 03:44.820
What?

03:44.820 --> 03:46.810
Never mind Nami.

03:47.320 --> 03:50.050
Oh, I see.

03:51.660 --> 03:53.420
She gets special treatment!

03:55.360 --> 03:57.160
Have it your way.

04:00.570 --> 04:03.870
Well! It's so kind of you to stop by!

04:03.870 --> 04:08.110
I thought I'd check in on you.
How are you feeling?

04:08.110 --> 04:10.980
I feel wonderful.

04:10.980 --> 04:14.850
I'm wearing the special charm
I was given, see?

04:14.850 --> 04:19.650
We look forward to your serving as an
attendant in the upcoming Advent Festival.

04:20.420 --> 04:22.050
I'm honored.

04:35.770 --> 04:38.830
Hey, you! What are you doing there?

04:39.470 --> 04:41.380
The Shichi-go-san candy...

04:41.380 --> 04:43.500
Huh? What're you talking about?!

04:44.080 --> 04:50.110
My daughter lost it somewhere,
and she won't stop crying.

04:53.660 --> 04:55.680
Hey, what's wrong? Are you okay?!

04:58.690 --> 05:00.920
Wh-What the hell?!

05:30.660 --> 05:32.290
Hello...

05:32.430 --> 05:35.120
Maya? You're awake, aren't you?

05:38.930 --> 05:40.560
Maya!

05:40.940 --> 05:42.730
I'm all right!

05:43.510 --> 05:46.070
I just got a little dizzy.

05:46.570 --> 05:49.300
It's all the preparations for the
Advent Festival, isn't it?

05:51.880 --> 05:57.150
I'm fine, really.
After all, I'm doing it for Mother.

05:59.350 --> 06:03.730
I don't think we should rush things.

06:03.730 --> 06:07.130
I'll talk to Sara.

06:07.130 --> 06:10.530
But I don't want to upset Mother!

06:10.530 --> 06:13.330
Don't you worry about that.

06:13.330 --> 06:16.460
You just relax and get some rest.

06:29.220 --> 06:31.710
What am I doing?

06:34.520 --> 06:37.010
I guess I'm a bit early.

06:38.330 --> 06:42.020
Sorry, my aunt's still out shopping!

06:42.630 --> 06:46.170
Why can't we make it public?
She's a friend of mine!

06:46.170 --> 06:47.900
Orders from above.

06:47.900 --> 06:49.200
Damn it...

06:49.200 --> 06:52.010
Kuroshio's little toady is here again.

06:52.010 --> 06:54.940
He's the boss's illegitimate son, no?

06:54.940 --> 06:57.580
Watch it, walls have ears!

06:57.580 --> 07:00.480
God forbid!

07:00.580 --> 07:04.110
Is that so? Mr. Kuroshio's that concerned?

07:04.690 --> 07:08.880
Well, I've arranged to keep it quiet for
"investigational purposes."

07:09.190 --> 07:10.820
Oh!

07:10.960 --> 07:15.490
I appreciate your understanding.
We're happy to offer our support.

07:15.960 --> 07:17.870
I do appreciate that.

07:17.870 --> 07:21.160
It's difficult to equip ourselves properly
with just city funding.

07:22.540 --> 07:26.210
I see, that's why you came back to Otomo?

07:26.210 --> 07:29.510
Does it surprise you that I have a child?

07:29.680 --> 07:35.510
But as far as he was concerned,
I was just a tool he needed to have a child.

07:36.580 --> 07:39.020
Where is she?

07:39.690 --> 07:44.520
The last I saw her was at the
Shichi-go-san Festival last year.

07:48.900 --> 07:50.520
Nami...

07:52.800 --> 07:56.500
About that promise I made...
It's not too late, is it?

07:58.540 --> 08:01.010
The promise I made when I left for Tokyo...

08:02.510 --> 08:05.100
Stop! Don't tease your elders!

08:05.410 --> 08:06.780
Nami, I...

08:06.780 --> 08:07.980
No!
Nami, I...

08:07.980 --> 08:11.180
The truth is, I...

08:21.060 --> 08:23.700
Yes? Oh?

08:23.700 --> 08:26.000
He didn't put up much of a fight!

08:27.240 --> 08:30.930
I see, show them to my office then.

08:32.270 --> 08:34.300
Yes, thank you.

08:37.550 --> 08:40.410
Mother, the time has finally come!

08:43.280 --> 08:45.720
So that means...

08:45.850 --> 08:49.620
We'd better split up tomorrow.

08:50.020 --> 08:52.430
You're sending me off alone?

08:52.430 --> 08:54.260
You'll be fine!

08:54.260 --> 08:58.030
After all, you've got that whole
"Hyaaa! Hyaaa!" thing going on!

09:00.270 --> 09:03.870
I see. Basically, it's like I'm
not even a girl, huh?

09:03.870 --> 09:05.500
Huh?

09:13.050 --> 09:15.780
Huh? You're still here?

09:15.780 --> 09:18.450
Well, I had to look into some stuff.

09:18.450 --> 09:21.720
Sure, whatever. Just clean up
that desk, will you?

09:22.020 --> 09:23.850
Hey, Yamagi?

09:24.590 --> 09:31.290
So, when they say three months' salary...

09:32.670 --> 09:34.290
Ah, there's a lady?

09:35.870 --> 09:37.960
I'm serious about this!

09:39.510 --> 09:41.700
Women are demons, pal!

10:04.370 --> 10:05.990
Gago?

10:06.770 --> 10:11.970
I see, that's your name for
the GRO series, is it?

10:13.010 --> 10:15.640
Well, it's just a nickname.

10:16.040 --> 10:20.850
Well, they were developed from the OPARTs
unearthed in this region,

10:20.850 --> 10:22.710
so I suppose it's only fair.

10:23.380 --> 10:25.720
I appreciate your understanding.

10:25.720 --> 10:27.350
By the by...

10:27.720 --> 10:32.320
I hear word you've got some
Lost Numbers hiding in the area.

10:33.760 --> 10:37.390
The experimental subjects from
the South Asian War?

10:38.970 --> 10:42.640
Is that so? That's the first I've heard of it.

10:42.640 --> 10:45.830
We'll look into it right away.

10:47.240 --> 10:50.480
I'm so glad we were able to meet today.

10:50.480 --> 10:52.880
As am I.

10:54.050 --> 10:58.590
If it's more than you can handle,
just say the word.

10:58.590 --> 11:01.560
We're good partners after all.

11:03.720 --> 11:05.560
Yes, of course.

11:12.230 --> 11:13.900
About the you-know-what...

11:13.900 --> 11:14.940
Hmm?

11:14.940 --> 11:17.400
Should I have it destroyed?

11:17.640 --> 11:19.570
It's beyond our control, yes?

11:19.570 --> 11:22.380
Yes, we're still looking into the cause,

11:22.380 --> 11:24.980
but it seems the test subject was problematic.

11:24.980 --> 11:28.940
In all things, haste makes waste.

11:30.320 --> 11:32.420
Well, I'll be going then.

11:32.420 --> 11:34.290
About the Gago Project...

11:34.290 --> 11:35.920
Hmm?

11:35.920 --> 11:38.450
Perhaps we should call it off.

11:39.030 --> 11:41.460
Because it's not a stable weapon?

11:43.760 --> 11:45.460
No, I'm speaking as a father.

11:45.770 --> 11:49.290
I understand, Sir.

12:05.520 --> 12:05.590
CLOSED

12:05.590 --> 12:07.890
CLOSED

12:05.590 --> 12:07.890
What? Nami's not coming in?!

12:07.890 --> 12:12.120
That's right, said she wasn't feeling well.

12:12.290 --> 12:16.130
I see. Is she okay?

12:16.360 --> 12:20.030
She said it was just a cold,
so I'm sure she'll be better soon.

12:20.030 --> 12:22.700
That's good. Well, I'll come back another time.

12:23.000 --> 12:24.670
Oh, wait!

12:24.670 --> 12:30.010
Are you Mr. Mikogami?
Or Mr. Shinjo? I forget...

12:30.010 --> 12:32.140
There's a letter from Nami.

12:32.410 --> 12:34.110
Oh...

12:35.180 --> 12:36.420
Minakami
Restaurant

12:36.420 --> 12:37.620
Minakami
Restaurant


12:36.420 --> 12:37.620
Damn! Why, Nami, why?

12:37.620 --> 12:39.890
Damn! Why, Nami, why?

12:39.890 --> 12:41.660
MR. HAYATO
MIKOGAMI

12:41.660 --> 12:44.890
Honestly, why do you think that is?

12:44.890 --> 12:48.330
Kiriko, this isn't a confession.

12:48.330 --> 12:50.800
But we're all equal in God's eyes, right?

12:52.070 --> 12:56.700
I guess I was dumb for ever
trusting a guy like him at all!

12:56.970 --> 13:01.870
But he could stand to have a little consideration
for a girl's feelings, that nincompoop!

13:02.580 --> 13:04.200
In other words...

13:04.910 --> 13:07.350
You like Hayato, don't you?

13:08.950 --> 13:12.650
I didn't say I have any problem with him
mooning over older women!

13:12.650 --> 13:17.420
You don't understand anything,
Father Kanzaki! Sheesh!

13:22.930 --> 13:26.330
What a laugh!
Where'd he get that idea, anyway?

13:38.550 --> 13:43.880
Yippee! I'm cooking tonight!

13:43.880 --> 13:45.940
Is that so?

13:55.260 --> 13:56.930
Come in.

13:56.930 --> 14:01.300
Thanks to the support of our major stockholder,
everything's going perfectly!

14:01.670 --> 14:04.300
You've done good work.

14:15.180 --> 14:16.480
MR. HAYATO
MIKOGAMI

14:38.770 --> 14:40.400
No...

14:59.890 --> 15:01.730
You're awake?

15:01.730 --> 15:04.330
I have to find her candy!

15:04.330 --> 15:07.600
Let me down! She's crying!

15:09.700 --> 15:14.080
I think I had another bad dream!

15:14.080 --> 15:18.010
What have I done?

15:18.010 --> 15:20.380
You haven't done anything.

15:20.750 --> 15:25.650
You just fainted in the street.

15:25.650 --> 15:30.390
No! That's not true! I think I...I...

15:30.890 --> 15:33.360
I'll protect you, Nami.

15:33.860 --> 15:37.230
So, don't worry about a thing.

15:39.330 --> 15:43.300
There is a face that God gives us,

15:43.300 --> 15:48.000
and a face we fashion ourselves.

15:48.440 --> 15:51.310
So, you're the real Skullman!

16:01.520 --> 16:03.750
Hayato! Where are you?

16:04.360 --> 16:06.760
What are you, anyway?!

16:07.030 --> 16:11.130
Gago, GRO or the Lost Numbers...

16:11.130 --> 16:15.260
No, none of those is our name.

16:15.670 --> 16:18.240
Our true name is...

16:18.240 --> 16:20.800
Servants of the Skull!

16:20.940 --> 16:22.600
No!

16:24.180 --> 16:25.540
Nami!

16:25.850 --> 16:29.110
Please! Don't look at me!

16:34.320 --> 16:36.480
Nami?

16:41.830 --> 16:43.890
The Phantom has appeared on 6th Street!

16:44.060 --> 16:48.000
Patrol car 28 has been attacked.
All cars report immediately!

16:49.870 --> 16:51.670
Shinjo, we're up.

16:51.970 --> 16:53.640
What's wrong?

16:53.640 --> 16:55.970
Nothing...Nothing's wrong.

16:57.510 --> 17:01.810
Why couldn't it have been me, Nami?

17:02.980 --> 17:04.810
I'm sorry.

17:06.550 --> 17:07.960
Somehow...

17:07.960 --> 17:09.920
I just couldn't tell you.

17:12.590 --> 17:16.150
I wanted to. I wanted you to know.

17:16.260 --> 17:19.660
I can't control myself.

17:20.000 --> 17:21.670
Hour by hour...

17:21.670 --> 17:24.160
I'm turning into something
other than myself.

17:46.330 --> 17:47.950
I'm scared.

17:48.360 --> 17:49.990
Scared!

17:50.400 --> 17:52.260
I'm frightened...

17:53.370 --> 17:55.700
...of myself!

18:03.510 --> 18:05.270
Car 13 here. Subject spotted!

18:05.480 --> 18:07.500
He's at the Otomo shopping street, headed
towards the Marutomo Department store...

18:14.220 --> 18:20.560
I know it's a selfish request.

18:21.260 --> 18:22.960
But...

18:24.900 --> 18:26.530
Fire!

18:27.100 --> 18:28.770
Men! Don't let them escape! Surround them!

18:28.770 --> 18:30.400
Yes, Sir!

18:38.180 --> 18:40.240
Save me!

18:40.350 --> 18:42.510
Save me, please!

18:44.520 --> 18:46.650
I'm sorry.

18:46.750 --> 18:49.220
I know it's crazy.

18:49.220 --> 18:50.850
Nami!

18:51.790 --> 18:54.230
Where are you?! Answer me!

18:59.230 --> 19:02.630
There's one last thing I want to tell you.

19:04.100 --> 19:06.540
I'm glad I met you.

19:09.880 --> 19:13.310
I'm glad I got to talk with you.

19:15.720 --> 19:17.780
Truly...

19:21.760 --> 19:23.750
Thank you.

19:25.130 --> 19:26.390
All officers, char...

19:26.390 --> 19:28.020
Chief!
All officers, char...

19:35.140 --> 19:38.000
The murderer, caught red-handed!
Arrest him!

19:38.570 --> 19:40.840
Don't get the wrong idea. It wasn't me.

19:40.840 --> 19:43.140
Don't listen! Get him!

19:45.150 --> 19:46.770
What the?!

20:09.300 --> 20:11.440
Nami...

20:11.440 --> 20:12.610
Who on earth...

20:12.610 --> 20:14.570
I saw it.

20:14.940 --> 20:17.340
The culprit was someone you know well.

20:17.340 --> 20:19.310
Who? Who was it?!

20:23.980 --> 20:27.960
Thank you for authorizing their use.

20:27.960 --> 20:33.090
They're not combat-ready yet,
but this is a good opportunity.

20:33.560 --> 20:35.500
Leave it to me.

20:35.500 --> 20:38.490
I promise you'll see excellent results.

20:49.880 --> 20:53.210
Well! Look at this!

20:53.780 --> 20:57.310
It seems the show is about to begin!

20:57.990 --> 21:01.580
I'd better hurry up and finish my work!

21:03.160 --> 21:12.260
There is only one sky,
though the world is large

21:12.400 --> 21:16.940
When you lose sight of the one you love

21:16.940 --> 21:22.530
Look up at it for strength

21:22.680 --> 21:31.820
The path we walked together
now splits into two

21:31.820 --> 21:40.660
Our tears show how much
we long to meet again

21:40.930 --> 21:45.500
The you of tomorrow will be born tomorrow

21:45.500 --> 21:50.670
Just as the Sun rises after a long night

21:50.670 --> 21:54.680
Throw away all the rest of the dream

21:54.680 --> 21:58.940
And open your arms!

21:59.180 --> 22:03.820
The future is always right before your eyes

22:03.820 --> 22:08.820
Just waiting for you to step forward

22:08.820 --> 22:12.930
Beyond the horizon

22:12.930 --> 22:20.730
A world awaits you, and new encounters

22:25.040 --> 22:25.410
Tenth Night


22:25.040 --> 22:25.410
The Circus Laughs at Midnight

22:25.410 --> 22:30.180
Tenth Night


22:25.410 --> 22:30.180
The Circus Laughs at Midnight

22:25.410 --> 22:30.180

The jesters laugh,
wandering in search of blood.

22:30.180 --> 22:37.480
Tenth Night


22:30.180 --> 22:37.480
The Circus Laughs at Midnight

22:30.180 --> 22:37.480

Soulless shells, denizens of Purgatory;
ignorant of what lies in store.

22:37.480 --> 22:38.210
Tenth Night


22:37.480 --> 22:38.210
The Circus Laughs at Midnight
